aarch64: widen pointer constants and synchronize C2 call return offsets

Combines the former 0019 movptr change and 0022 C2 return-PC correction.
The code changes are retained together: emitting a longer sequence without
updating the return-PC metadata breaks OopMap and debug-scope lookup.

movptr() used three instructions and dropped everything above bit 47, which
on Android includes the top-byte heap-pointer tag.  Emit a fourth instruction
and update the constant reader, patcher and NativeMovConstReg::instruction_size
to 16 bytes.

The dynamic Java call returns after movptr plus BL: 16 + 4 = 20 bytes.
The external runtime call returns after ADR, movptr, STP and BLR:
4 + 16 + 4 + 4 = 28 bytes.  Express both offsets using the sequence-size
constant instead of the old 16/24-byte literals.  A generated-code runtime
call site remains one BL in both near and far trampoline modes, so its return
offset is always one instruction; far mode only changes the out-of-line target.

Apply after 0017/0018, then apply 0020 for the fixed stub layouts and 0021
for the existing conditional fourth-word handling.  This patch alone is not
the complete layout migration.

Built and run on device with the rest of this series: java -version reports
mixed mode, javac H.java finishes in 0.19s at 251% CPU, java H prints ok and
a -Xmx16m run performs four young collections. A single javac timing is a
sample, not a benchmark or a proof of coverage.

